{"additions":179,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTkyMzQy","is_bot":false,"login":"shrirajh","name":""},"body":"# Objective\r\n\r\n- Zed stores every string-form lifecycle command as `/bin/sh -c <script>`, even on Windows.\r\n- The [dev container specification](https://containers.dev/implementors/json_reference/#lifecycle-scripts) says that `initializeCommand` is the only lifecycle command that runs on the host machine.\r\n- Windows does not have `/bin/sh`, and it reads the path as `C:\\bin\\sh`.\r\n- The dev container fails before Zed starts Docker:\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR [dev_container::devcontainer_json] Error running command default: The system cannot find the path specified. (os error 3)\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\n- On Windows, Zed runs a string-form host script with `%ComSpec% /C <script>`.\r\n- Zed adds the script with `raw_arg`, because `cmd` reads the quotes from `arg` as normal text.\r\n- Container commands do not change, and array-form commands run directly.\r\n- The current fix surgically swaps `/bin/sh -c` for `%ComSpec% /C`, but the stored data is **still not correct**.\r\n- ***The better fix is to correct the stored data***, but that changes the public `LifecycleScript` type, its `Serialize` and `PartialEq` behavior, and its constructors.\r\n- I am an external contributor, and I feel that the above larger change is a decision for the Zed team.\r\n- A merge of this fix helps Windows users now, and it gives the Zed team time to plan the larger change.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n- I added three unit tests to `devcontainer_json.rs`.\r\n- One test starts `cmd.exe` and shows that `cmd` receives `echo \"hello world\"` with the correct quotes.\r\n- I tested on Windows 11, and the unit tests, `./script/clippy`, and `cargo fmt --check` show no errors.\r\n- I did not test on macOS or Linux, where the behavior does not change.\r\n- To test by hand, put a string `initializeCommand` in `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json`, and then open the folder in a dev container.\r\n\r\n## Self-Review Checklist:\r\n\r\n- [x] I've reviewed my own diff for quality, security, and reliability\r\n- [x] Unsafe blocks (if any) have justifying comments\r\n- [x] The content adheres to Zed's UI standards ([UX/UI](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#uiux-checklist) and [icon](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/main/crates/icons/README.md) guidelines)\r\n- [x] Tests cover the new/changed behavior\r\n- [x] Performance impact has been considered and is acceptable\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRelease Notes:\r\n\r\n- Fixed dev containers that do not start on Windows when `devcontainer.json` gives `initializeCommand` as a string\r\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-29T00:16:43Z","deletions":10,"files":[{"path":"crates/dev_container/src/devcontainer_json.rs","additions":169,"deletions":10,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/util/src/command.rs","additions":10,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"}],"isDraft":false,"labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOFExXwM8AAAABgYGhPg","name":"cla-signed","description":"The user has signed the Contributor License Agreement","color":"ededed"},{"id":"LA_kwDOFExXwM8AAAACSvx30Q","name":"area:dev containers","description":"Feedback for Zed's dev containers feature","color":"2eaafb"},{"id":"LA_kwDOFExXwM8AAAACS5igiQ","name":"first contribution","description":"the author's first pull request to Zed. NOTE: the label application is automated via github actions","color":"8de988"}],"mergedAt":null,"number":63391,"reviews":[],"state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T02:17:57Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/actions/runs/33223074554/job/99362043501","name":"build_nix_linux_x86_64","startedAt":"2026-08-31T02:17:58Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"nix_build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T02:17:56Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/actions/runs/33350235019/job/993620